---
import ProviderPlaybookTemplate from '../components/ProviderPlaybookTemplate.astro';
const data = {
 "kind": "connect",
 "name": "Wix",
 "title": "How to Connect a Domain to Wix",
 "description": "Point your custom domain to Wix: exact records, method choice, and verification.",
 "intro": "Connecting an existing domain to Wix takes two DNS changes done carefully. Here is the exact method and the verification step.",
 "steps": [
  [
   "Get Wix's values",
   "Wix, Domains: either point nameservers to NS1.wixdns.net / NS2.wixdns.net (recommended) or use the Pointing method with Wix's displayed A/AAAA values."
  ],
  [
   "Publish at the registrar",
   "Set the nameservers or the A records per the chosen method."
  ],
  [
   "Verify in Wix",
   "Wix checks and shows the domain connected; SSL is then provisioned automatically."
  ]
 ],
 "quirk": "Wix's Pointing method only covers the homepage well; the nameserver method is Wix's recommended path because it lets them manage records for you.",
 "faqs": [
  [
   "How long until my Wix site loads on my domain?",
   "Up to 48 hours after nameserver changes, usually much less. Check propagation with the checker."
  ],
  [
   "How long do DNS changes take in Wix?",
   "The provider serves new values quickly, but resolvers keep old answers until each record's TTL expires. Verify live values with the record lookup, then watch the propagation checker until resolvers agree."
  ],
  [
   "Where do I find Wix's nameservers?",
   "This playbook's nameservers guide covers the exact location. They are the delegation pair your registrar must point at for {name} to be authoritative."
  ],
  [
   "Should I lower TTL before changing records in Wix?",
   "Yes, for anything planned: set TTL to 300 seconds at least one old-TTL cycle ahead, make the change, confirm propagation, then restore the TTL."
  ],
  [
   "Can I keep email with one provider and DNS in Wix?",
   "Yes: DNS host and mail provider are independent. Publish the mail provider's MX, SPF, DKIM, and DMARC records in {name}, and keep those records unproxied."
  ]
 ],
 "related": [
  [
   "DNS record types reference",
   "/dns-records/"
  ],
  [
   "TTL explained",
   "/what-is-ttl-in-dns/"
  ]
 ]
};
---
<ProviderPlaybookTemplate data={data} />
